{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":6292,"ns":0,"title":"Convex set","extract":"In geometry, a set of points is convex if it contains every line segment between two points in the set.\nFor example, a solid cube is a convex set, but anything that is hollow or has an indent, such as a crescent shape, is not convex.","description":"In geometry, set whose intersection with every line is a single line segment","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}